    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d489">

                <pb facs="0535" n="529" sameAs="frus:frus1894app1/pg529"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Sir Julian Pauncefote
                        to Mr. Blaine.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-04-28"><hi rendition="#italic">April 28,
                        1892</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that Her
                    Majesty’s consul at Samoa has forwarded to the Marquis of Salisbury a letter
                    from Mr. Robert Louis Stevenson, inclosing certain proposals for the amendment
                    of the final act of the Berlin conference, which have been drawn up by a
                    committee at Apia and adopted at a meeting of the foreign residents.</p>
                <p>In accordance with instructions which I have received from my Government, I have
                    the honor to transmit to you herewith for the consideration of the United States
                    Government copies of this correspondence, together with a copy of the final act
                    showing the alterations which have been suggested.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Julian
                    Pauncefote.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
